  "description": "Supabase Auth for the DDDToolkit, in any host: validates the access tokens Supabase Auth issues against the keys the project publishes, or its JWT secret, and turns a valid one into the caller whose role and claims row level security applies to the application's queries. DDDToolkit.Auth.Supabase.AspNetCore and DDDToolkit.Auth.Supabase.AzureFunctions put it in front of a request. For server code it also has a client for Auth's admin API: make a user under a given id, invite an address, and find or delete a user by id.",
